<h1>Enforcement actions</h1>
    <div class="lead-paragraph">
        <p data-block-key="eydlt">When we take an enforcement action against an entity or person we believe has violated the law, we will post court documents and other related materials here.</p>
    </div>
    <p data-block-key="wwa9b">The Bureau may enforce the law by filing an action in federal district court or by initiating an administrative adjudication proceeding. Administrative proceedings are conducted by an Administrative Law Judge, who holds hearings and issues a recommended decision. Proceedings are conducted in accordance with the <a class="a-link" href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-12/chapter-X/part-1081?toc=1"><span class="a-link__text">Rules of Practice for Adjudication Proceedings</span> <cfpb-icon name="external-link"></cfpb-icon></a>.</p>
